{
  "requirement": "The agent's `read_source` tool accepts a project-relative file path and an\noptional outline selector. An omitted or empty selector identifies the whole file.\nThe project-relative path and selector identify an `OutlineId` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`. The Rust operation accepts the\n`OutlineId` directly. It maps that outline identity into the application's\ngraph, then obtains its node contents through `Domain::node_content`.\nThe selected file belongs to the project scope under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. Mapping and read failures\nreturn errors.\n\nThe Rust caller receives `D::NodeContent`; the agent receives those same\ncontents presented by `NodeContents::format` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `read_source.behavior`.\n\n**Whole-file default.** `omitted_and_explicit_empty_selectors_deliver_the_same_whole_file` in `project_sources.rs` reads once with the selector omitted and once with `\"\"`. It asserts the same node address (`path` plus empty `selector`), the same text, and the same dependency each time.\n\n**Agent and Rust inputs map to an `OutlineId`.**\n- `fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies` dispatches `read_source` and checks the result. The text is the domain's \"prepared domain contents\", not the disk text \"disk text\".\n- It also checks that the dependency is `Node(\"source-node\", Content.fingerprint())`, which shows the read went through `Domain::node_content`.\n- `direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns` calls `inspection.read_source(&OutlineId)` directly, so the Rust operation takes an `OutlineId`.\n- It returns the domain content, and `returned.format()` equals \"prepared contents\".\n- `read_nodes` records `source-node`, which shows the mapped node was read.\n\n**Selector forwarding.**\n- The test domain's `source_node` supports only `source.txt` with an empty selector.\n- The direct test passes `line[unknown]` and the unknown path `unknown.txt`. Both fail with \"unsupported source item\", and no read occurs (`reads == 0`).\n- The dispatch test passes selectors `line[unknown]` and `fn[unclosed`. Both return errors.\n- A non-empty selector is therefore passed to the mapping step. If it were dropped, those reads would succeed.\n\n**Project scope, from the cited `local_provider`.**\n- The dispatch test reads a `.gitignore`d `ignored.txt` and `../source.txt`. Both return errors, and the read count stays at 1.\n- `supplied_agent_uses_attached_project_tools_in_both_configuration_orders` in `configured.rs` goes through a real agent loop. It reads an ignored file, and the output contains \"excluded\".\n- It then reads a visible file and gets the domain snapshot, not the disk contents. It does this in both configuration orders and with a different decoy project attached.\n\n**Mapping and read failures return errors.** The direct test and `fixed_source_reads_redact_delivery_and_propagate_preparation_errors` set `fail_read` and assert the \"prepared source read failed\" error. The direct test also asserts that failed attempts record no dependencies.\n\n**The caller gets `D::NodeContent`; the agent gets `NodeContents::format` output.**\n- The direct test checks `returned.format()` and `returned.fingerprint()`.\n- The dispatch tests check the delivered text. A text file gives `mapped[\"text\"] == \"a source snapshot\"`.\n- The long-text case checks that the paged retained text is the formatted content, with \"é\" repeated 20,000 times.\n- The retained text is unchanged after the domain changes.\n- This also supports \"formatting uses the retained value without further reads\": the read count stays at 3 across the paged reads.\n\n**Gaps.**\n- I found none. Only a successful read with a non-empty selector against the domain is not exercised in the new `OutlineId` tests. Its mapping is the domain's responsibility under `source_nodes`, and selector forwarding is already shown by the failing cases.\n- Nested ignore exceptions and Git metadata exclusion belong to `local_provider`'s own tests. They are not reassessed here.",
  "references": "facfbc9a8f72079bd8775dedea4d4084dffc2a0b60f9abcebba6427de9fb0e98",
